n-social","label":"Open social presence (Mastodon/Bluesky) linked","pass":false,"detail":""}],"passed":8,"total":11,"social":[],"og":{"title":"Broadband Wireless Access and Applications Center (BWAC)","description":"The Broadband Wireless Access and Applications Center (BWAC) aims to advance wireless technologies and provide cost-effective and practical solutions for next-generation communications system (5G and beyond) through novel broadband technologies.BWAC's mission is to collaborate with industry research partners to create flexible, efficient, and secure wireless systems that satisfy broadband communication needs by pursuing large-scale research programs and creating new visions for the wireless industry.BWAC addresses fundamental research challenges in next-generation wireless systems. The intertwined and multifaceted nature of such complex systems calls for a diverse range of complementary expertise in antenna design, radio engineering, signal processing, wireless communications, networking, cloud computing, and security, as well as research tools (modeling, simulation, hardware/software prototyping, platform integration and maintenance, and measurements and data curation). The breadth of such a research program necessitates collaboration among multiple research teams and partnering with pioneering private companies and federal agencies in this field.","url":"/centers/broadband-wireless-access-and-applications-center/","image":"/assets/images/twittercard.png","siteName":null,"type":"article"},"resilience":{"checks":[{"id":"pwa-https","label":"HTTPS (required for service workers)","status":"pass","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/broadband-wireless-access-and-applications-center/","why":"HTTPS is required for service workers and most install prompts."},{"id":"pwa-manifest","label":"Web app manifest declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/broadband-wireless-access-and-applications-center/","w